  "description": "Hosts one Model Context Protocol (MCP) server inside an ABP Framework application and lets any number of ABP modules contribute tools, resources and prompts to it. Owns everything that exists once per server - Streamable HTTP transport, the /mcp endpoint, ABP-permission filtering of tools/list, one structured error envelope, server info and composed instructions - and enforces that each contributing module stays inside its own name prefix and resource URI scheme, failing at startup on any collision. Domain-agnostic - not owned by, and does not reference, any module in this repository.",
